@anon.8ad231a129453d088979dfad2582f60a.1466 = private unnamed_addr constant [1455 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for the presence of unnecessary quotes in type annotations.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIn Python, type annotations can be quoted to avoid forward references.\0A\0AHowever, if `from __future__ import annotations` is present, Python\0Awill always evaluate type annotations in a deferred manner, making\0Athe quotes unnecessary.\0A\0ASimilarly, if the annotation is located in a typing-only context and\0Awon't be evaluated by Python at runtime, the quotes will also be\0Aconsidered unnecessary. For example, Python does not evaluate type\0Aannotations on assignments in function bodies.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0AGiven:\0A\0A```python\0Afrom __future__ import annotations\0A\0A\0Adef foo(bar: \22Bar\22) -> \22Bar\22: ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Afrom __future__ import annotations\0A\0A\0Adef foo(bar: Bar) -> Bar: ...\0A```\0A\0AGiven:\0A\0A```python\0Adef foo() -> None:\0A    bar: \22Bar\22\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Adef foo() -> None:\0A    bar: Bar\0A```\0A\0A## See also\0A- [`quoted-annotation-in-stub`][PYI020]: A rule that\0A  removes all quoted annotations from stub files\0A- [`quoted-type-alias`][TC008]: A rule that removes unnecessary quotes\0A  from type aliases.\0A\0A## References\0A- [PEP 563 \E2\80\93 Postponed Evaluation of Annotations](https://peps.python.org/pep-0563/)\0A- [Python documentation: `__future__`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/__future__.html#module-__future__)\0A\0A[PYI020]: https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/quoted-annotation-in-stub/\0A[TC008]: https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/quoted-type-alias/\0A", align 1
