@anon.8ad231a129453d088979dfad2582f60a.1474 = private unnamed_addr constant [495 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of hardcoded charsets, which are defined in Python string module.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AUsage of named charsets from the standard library is more readable and less error-prone.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Ax = \220123456789\22\0Ay in \22abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz\22\0A```\0A\0AUse instead\0A```python\0Aimport string\0A\0Ax = string.digits\0Ay in string.ascii_lowercase\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: String constants](https://docs.python.org/3/library/string.html#string-constants)\0A", align 1
